# ProfileCard Component Rules

## Product Overview
[TBD — Describe the overall feel and purpose of the ProfileCard.]

## Props
- `name` (string) – User's display name
- `title` (string) – Role or subtitle (e.g., "Designer & Engineer")
- `bio` (string) – Short description
- `avatarUrl` (optional string) – Image URL; fallback to blank circle when absent

## Typography
Use intentional, hierarchy-driven typography:
- **Name**: `text-2xl` or `text-3xl`, `font-bold` or `font-semibold`, `tracking-tight`, `text-white`
- **Title**: `text-sm`, `font-medium` or `font-normal`, `text-zinc-400`
- **Bio**: `text-sm`, `leading-relaxed`, `text-zinc-300`

Avoid `font-black` and `font-light` extremes unless explicitly required for the design system.

## Layout & Spacing
- Card: `max-w-md`, `rounded-2xl`, `p-6`
- Avatar: `h-14 w-14`, `rounded-full`
- Gap between avatar and content: `gap-4`
- Bio margin-top: `mt-5`
- Buttons: `mt-6`, `gap-2`

## Buttons
- Primary (Follow): filled, high contrast
- Secondary (Message): bordered, lower emphasis
- Both: `rounded-lg`, `px-3 py-2`, `text-sm`

## Theme
- Background: `bg-zinc-950`
- Card: `bg-zinc-900/40`, `border-zinc-800`
- Keep the dark, neutral palette (zinc) consistent
